        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "By the impugned common judgement dated 23.10.2021, the learned ASJ dismissed the Criminal Appeal No. 109/2019 filed by the petitioner husband and allowed Criminal Appeal No. 133/2019 filed by the respondent wife, modifying the judgement dat"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "df1d0ba87bc74dcfa53d2178c16cb5e9_5",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 102,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "4. Dissatisfied with this award, the petitioner husband filed Criminal Appeal No. 109/2019 seeking to set aside the impugned judgement dated 22.04.2019 and the respondent wife filed Criminal Appeal No. 133/2019 seeking enhancement, leading "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "650c4d01132c4666a5ac424d91e4ce1f_6",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The learned ASJ awarded the following reliefs to the respondent wife:\n5.1. Maintenance for the child, who by now has attained the age of majority, to the tune of 25,000/- per month, from the date filing of the petition, till the said child "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2c1e58fe6ec547f5933bee3e342ac03b_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "16. The impugned orders have come to be passed, after appreciation of the Domestic Incident Report and holding the respondent wife to be an 'aggrieved person' in terms of Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005 (DV Act) and the"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "50dc150aca164990bba4a761d4144ab5_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "17. The ASJ observed that the respondent wife while doing a job, wherein she was earning about 6.5 lakhs to 7 lakhs per year, had single headedly brought up her minor child and taken care of his day-to-day requirements towards his education"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "add9dc2ddf4348c297e9a443d81c9924_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Moreover, she has run pillar to post in order to save the shared premises which was mortgaged by the petitioner husband with the bank."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5b15d138f3b64e669a2e121af176fc17_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "18. The petitioner husband has though denied any violence, however, from the perusal of the record, it is evident that he played little role in supporting and providing for his wife and minor child, rather he has made it only more difficult"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6cd0575bfe3045f387170322fc96c4c0_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The same led to the Courts below awarding the maintenance as mentioned above."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5565501871e44ebe97526de23d0e97f8_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n19. It is trite law that not providing any maintenance to the wife is a form of 'economic abuse' under the DV Act, Section 3(iv) defines economic abuse as:\n\"economic abuse\" includes-- (a) deprivation of all or any economic or financial res"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "247bec3d34a44cbdb2f8a7b933c8f961_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n20. A coordinate bench of this court in Ajay Kumar v. Uma:\n2024:DHC:80 made observation regarding the scope of the word 'Domestic Violence', the same has been reproduced below:\n\"The 'domestic relationship' between the petitioner and compla"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bdcdcd658c9d4a2fa1e515e722f9fef6_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nFurther the same includes physical, sexual, verbal, 'emotional' and 'economic' abuse."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8610351ab7214b9e9575c170e88e23ce_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe object safeguard the rights of the women who are victims of violence of any kind occurring within the family, and for matters connected therewith or incidentally thereof.\"\n21."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fb31e6e1664e426390425a82020aed58_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The learned ASJ prima facie assessed the monthly income of the petitioner husband to be not less 1,25,000/- per month, based on his rental and miscellaneous expenses, and directed him to pay 25,000/- per month as maintenance for the child, "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7c193420571a433fa2e60c66693c1e72_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nSatyavol Venkat Rama Krishna Rao vs Kavita Rao on 17 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/186431079/\n4 22."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "49625ca763804239973bdc9ff8d13817_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The maintenance of 25,000/- has been awarded while assessing the monthly income of the petitioner husband to be not less than 1,25,000/- per month."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "05805f5920734b13a13b04ff5014c326_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The petitioner husband has not challenged the assessment of his income by the Courts below but has challenged the impugned order, contending that the amount awarded is on the higher side."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b892cea9ae3c4d848a9591ce5f78c8f3_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "23. The purpose of maintenance is to ensure the financial sustenance of the dependent spouse or child, while balancing the earning capacity of the abled party."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8e038f813c76477aa0cab1a93f1c9799_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Maintenance is not merely for survival but is aimed at ensuring a dignified existence, consistent with the standard of living enjoyed during the subsistence of the marriage."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3efd37fb1dc5436fa25f00914b346dcf_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "24. The learned ASJ rightly noted that the child will be completing his graduation/ Engineering till he turns 22-23 years of age and therefore he cannot be expected to start earning immediately after attaining the age of majority, to should"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5c37dc2c643243b69cfa2c79d05f6f3c_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Hon'ble Apex Court in a number of cases, has upheld and allowed the arrangement to provide maintenance to the son, even after the age of majority has been attained by him, as per facts and circumstances of the case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "149ba73a745b48d98bf17f1378bc0d1e_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "[Ref: Chandrashekhar v Swapnil, Criminal Appeal Nos. 265-266 of 2021; Rita Dutta v Subendhu Datta, (2005) 6 SCC 619]\n25."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1a84d3a89aa34deaadb4d329db5c252d_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The learned ASJ vide the impugned common judgement dated 23.10.2021 proportionately granted compensation to the tune of 10,00,000/- for expenses incurred by the respondent wife for the efforts made by her to protect the shared premises and "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7868c7de78114063b5460e55ea4e769c_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is settled law that the Court can grant monetary relief and/or compensation in terms of Sections 20 and 22 of the DV Act, at the stage of final disposal of the case, while taking in consideration, all evidence placed before it.\n"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4d4f858f14d044f9b31381df21f0b6cb_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "26. The learned ASJ has further granted relief of residence to the petitioner, with respect to the shared premises, as the fact that the same is the shared household of the respondent wife, has not been disproved by the petitioner husband."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "dfc612c8b3ea4f1d87e2110ae3761c1d_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The learned ASJ appropriately observed that the learned MM, while allowing the petitioner husband to sell the shared premises to a suitable buyer in order to execute the right of lien of the respondent wife, failed to consider the future ri"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1607aafe460d4aeb8ef52c04d80423c5_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The directions passed by the learned ASJ in order to protect the lien and right of residence need not be interfered with and are in consonance with the provision of Section 19 of the DV Act, by which the Court may impose any additional cond"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a8d16d8768414d17aee362f9fc8e3464_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "27. Furthermore, it is relevant to note that the reliefs under the DV Act can be granted if the complaint prima facie discloses that the respondent has committed an act of domestic violence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "18e471739c9e432c848cd8c320ac0e7f_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Any woman who proves that she has suffered domestic violence at the hands of her spouse/ partner, is entitled for such relief."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c051a788fc034c5483f79e1225b3f188_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, both the learned Trial Court as well as the learned ASJ has explicitly recorded that prima facie it appears from the complaint that the respondent was subjected to domestic violence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "267d13d0b8724887ba60f966dfc09f34_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nSatyavol Venkat Rama Krishna Rao vs Kavita Rao on 17 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/186431079/\n5 28."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8b7a37138db34d60b0908bd2b2271b9a_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Considering the facts as noted by the learned ASJ as well as the learned MM, this Court is of the opinion that the claims of the petitioner husband that it was not only the responsibility of the father,\nbut also of the mother to maintain th"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f96d7b412b024473a46498b52f1dfd47_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The duty of the husband to provide for his child persists regardless of any purported grievances."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a5067f6c497743e588e04d0f54386f33_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is trite that mere potential of the wife to provide for the child, is not sufficient to exempt the petitioner/husband, who is an able-bodied man, from financially supporting his child."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "296f368bdd6f44328cf3a03357bcd054_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "29. The learned counsel for the petitioner husband submits that in compliance with this Court's order dated 17.05.2024, the petitioner/ husband has paid a sum of 5,00,000/- to the respondent/\nwife, however no proof of the same has been plac"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ed6eb72f084948f385e0dd4f5fb94355_51",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "30. In view of the above, this Court finds no reason to interfere with the impugned judgements, and the petitions are dismissed in the aforesaid terms."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "34929e60cbad475595adb5fdb04d677e_52",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
